## Behaviour and content

The identity link returns to the service’s genuine home page. Do not use it to refresh the current route, open a menu or launch a device action. A long service name wraps without compressing the artwork. Keep the logo’s aspect ratio, clear space and supplied on-primary variant.

Do not include a crown, GOV.UK logotype, NHS logo or a government ownership statement. Do not create a second logo by typesetting the brand name. Branding rules also apply to standalone previews and error pages.

## Accessibility and testing

Give the identity image the concise alternative “civica.uk”. The surrounding link must have a meaningful destination. Check contrast and focus on every palette, and verify that the header does not obscure the skip link at high zoom. A service name is supporting context; the content still needs its own main heading.

## Home Assistant boundary and source

The companion’s own branding adapter has a separate compatibility contract. These HTML examples do not replace native HA routing. The structural reference is [GOV.UK Generic header](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/generic-header/); artwork comes from the supplied civica.uk V3.2 assets.
